; ─── THE HOSTAGE PIT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; One question: does an enemy holding the way UP create more stakes than an
; enemy holding some coins?
;
; So the level is arranged so the platform is the ONLY route to the exit. The
; upper deck sits at y=12 over a floor at y=0, with a 10 m trench between the
; two halves of the ground, and nothing to climb. Throw the seed in the trench,
; a platform manifests, ride it up. Let a snatcher take the seed and the exit is
; simply not available until you kill it.
;
; The trench is lethal rather than just deep — the hazard at the bottom is why
; you throw the seed in instead of climbing down after it. Note the hazard only
; ever touches the player, so neither the seed nor a snatcher is destroyed down
; there; the socket covers the whole trench floor for exactly that reason, so
; anything that ends up in the pit still counts as delivered.
[node name="HostagePit" type="Node3D"]

